      "content": "That's a very clear picture. I'm curious about how this applies to our global talent pool, though. We have some incredibly high-performing candidates from various cultural backgrounds—like East Asia or West Africa—who might have different ways of showing respect or authority. When we're screening, are there certain cultural communication styles or even physical mannerisms that we should be cautious about because they might be perceived as lacking that \"executive presence\" or \"commanding authority\" you described?",
